ific event instance. If you\u0027re also sending events via the Meta Pixel (browser-side), providing the same `event_id` for the same event sent via both Pixel and CAPI allows Meta to deduplicate them.\n    *   **`opt_out` (Optional):** Boolean. Set to `true` if the user has opted out of tracking for this event.\n\n4.  **`test_event_code` (Optional, for Testing):** When testing, you can get a test code from your Pixel\u0027s \"Test Events\" tab in Events Manager. Including this sends the event to the test tool instead of affecting your live data.\n\n**Prerequisites:**\n\n1.  **Meta Business Account:** You need one.\n2.  **Meta Pixel:** Create one in your Events Manager if you haven\u0027t already. Note down the **Pixel ID**.\n3.  **Access Token:**\n    *   Go to Events Manager.\n    *   Select your Pixel.\n    *   Go to the \"Settings\" tab.\n    *   Scroll down to \"Conversions API\" and click \"Generate access token\" under \"Set up manually.\"\n    *   **Copy this token and store it securely. It\u0027s like a password.**\n\n**Example: Sending a \"Purchase\" Event (Python)**\n\nLet\u0027s say a user just completed a purchase on your site.\n\n```python\nimport requests\nimport time\nimport hashlib\nimport json\n\n# --- CONFIGURATION ---\nPIXEL_ID \u003d \"YOUR_PIXEL_ID\"  # Replace with your Pixel ID\nACCESS_TOKEN \u003d \"YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN\" # Replace with your CAPI Access Token\n# For testing, get this from Events Manager \u003e Your Pixel \u003e Test Events\n# TEST_EVENT_CODE \u003d \"TESTXXXXX\" # Uncomment and use for testing\n\n# --- USER \u0026 EVENT DATA (This would come from your system) ---\nuser_email \u003d \"user@example.com\"\nuser_phone \u003d \"+11234567890\" # E.164 format recommended\nuser_ip_address \u003d \"123.123.123.123\" # User\u0027s actual IP\nuser_agent \u003d \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) ...\" # User\u0027s actual User Agent\nevent_url \u003d \"https://www.yoursite.com/thank-you-page\"\norder_id \u003d \"ORDER_12345\"\npur